ers; this heterogeneity is accounted for via position controls in the adjusted model", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position heterogeneity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 85, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[151, 152]], "note": "5.4 subheading"}, {"id": 86, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 158]], "assertion": "unadjusted RD increases with exposure: all dyads 0.20, ≥2 games 0.34, ≥5 games 0.46pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exposure restriction", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 87, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 160]], "assertion": "the effect is larger with more games, suggesting it is not driven by single-game outliers and may accumulate with exposure", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exposure"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 88, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[161, 163]], "note": "section separator with surrounding blanks"}, {"id": 89, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[164, 165]], "note": "Section 6 heading"}, {"id": 90, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[166, 167]], "note": "6.1 subheading"}, {"id": 91, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "inter-rater reliability was high (r=0.923) and coding was independent and blind to the research question", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inter-rater reliability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 92, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "caveat that photo-based skin tone may not reflect in-game appearance"}, {"id": 93, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "dichotomizing skin tone into light vs dark discards information from the excluded middle range, though it creates clearer comparison groups", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone dichotomization"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 94, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[171, 173]], "note": "6.2 subheading"}, {"id": 95, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "14.7% of dyads lack skin tone ratings, creating potential selection bias since missing players may differ systematically from those with photos", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing skin tone data"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 96, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "missing position data (6.9%) is judged low and unlikely to substantially bias results", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing position data"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 97, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[176, 178]], "note": "6.3 subheading"}, {"id": 98, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "lead-in to unmeasured confounders list"}, {"id": 99, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "player behavior/aggression not directly measured beyond yellow card proxy"}, {"id": 100, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "referee-specific implicit bias measures unavailable, only country-level aggregates"}, {"id": 101, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "lack of game context data (importance, score, home/away)"}, {"id": 102, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "player reputation/star treatment not accounted for"}, {"id": 103, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 186]], "assertion": "if dark-skinned players engage in more aggressive play beyond what yellow cards capture, this could confound the result, but the yellow card adjustment should account for much of it", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["unmeasured confounding"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 104, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[187, 188]], "note": "6.4 subheading"}, {"id": 105, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "observational cross-sectional design cannot definitively establish causation"}, {"id": 106, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "residual confounding by unmeasured factors could explain part or all of the association"}, {"id": 107, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[191, 192]], "note": "results consistent with differential treatment but alternative explanations not fully ruled out"}, {"id": 108, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[193, 194]], "note": "6.5 subheading"}, {"id": 109, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[195, 195]], "assertion": "the data are at the player-referee dyad level, not individual games", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["unit of analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 110, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[196, 196]], "assertion": "dyad-level aggregation reduces noise from single-game variability", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dyad aggregation"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 111, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "dyad aggregation prevents examining game-level factors like referee mood"}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[198, 199]], "assertion": "cluster-robust standard errors were used to mitigate non-independence of dyads from the same player", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cluster-robust standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[200, 201]], "note": "6.6 subheading"}, {"id": 114, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[202, 202]], "note": "lead-in listing logistic regression assumptions"}, {"id": 115, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "age/games may have non-linear effects on the logit scale, though they appear monotonic in exploratory analyses"}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[204, 204]], "assertion": "no perfect multicollinearity was found; VIFs were reasonable (not shown)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["multicollinearity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[205, 205]], "note": "marginal standardization assumes correct model specification"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "bootstrap validity assumption reasonable given N=100,135"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[207, 209]], "note": "section separator with surrounding blanks"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[210, 211]], "note": "Section 7 heading"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[212, 213]], "note": "Magnitude and Practical Significance subheading"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 215]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference of 0.26pp is small in absolute terms but meaningful in context", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 123, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 216]], "assertion": "baseline risk is 1.2% for light-skinned player-referee dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["baseline risk"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 124, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[217, 217]], "assertion": "relative increase is 22% higher risk for dark-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["relative risk increase"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 219]], "assertion": "population impact is roughly 46 excess red cards attributable to skin tone differences, based on ~17,490 dark-skinned dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["population impact"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[220, 221]], "assertion": "given red cards' substantial consequences, the modest effect size has meaningful implications for career outcomes and competitive fairness", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["practical significance"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[222, 223]], "note": "Comparison to Prior Literature subheading"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[224, 224]], "note": "comparison to prior literature on implicit racial bias in refereeing and other high-stakes decisions"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[225, 226]], "note": "Mechanisms subheading"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[227, 229]], "note": "lead-in to potential mechanisms list"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "speculative mechanism: implicit bias"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[231, 231]], "note": "speculative mechanism: stereotype threat, deemed less plausible"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[232, 232]], "note": "speculative mechanism: visibility/salience"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[233, 233]], "assertion": "league heterogeneity (positive in England/Germany, negative in France/Spain) suggests cultural context matters", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league heterogeneity", "mechanism"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[234, 236]], "note": "Policy Implications subheading"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[237, 238]], "note": "lead-in to policy intervention list"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[239, 239]], "assertion": "referee implicit bias training is suggested as a potential intervention", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["referee training"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[240, 240]], "assertion": "VAR technology is suggested as a way to reduce bias", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["VAR"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[241, 241]], "assertion": "monitoring and accountability tracking of referee decisions is suggested", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["monitoring"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[242, 242]], "assertion": "further experimental research is suggested to isolate causal mechanisms", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future research"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[243, 245]], "note": "section separator with surrounding blanks"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[246, 247]], "note": "Section 8 heading"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[248, 249]], "assertion": "conclusion stated as SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[250, 251]], "assertion": "the hypothesis that referees favor red cards against dark-skinned players is supported by the data", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[252, 253]], "assertion": "after adjustment, dark-skinned players face a 0.26pp higher probability (CI[0.03,0.57], p=0.028) and a 23% increase in odds (OR=1.23, CI[1.02,1.49])", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 255]], "assertion": "the effect is modest but meaningful, a 22% relative increase, with the CI excluding zero at alpha=0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [147, 148]}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 255]], "assertion": "the finding is robust to alternative skin tone definitions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [146, 148]}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 255]], "assertion": "the finding is not explained by measured confounders", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounders"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [146, 147]}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[256, 256]], "note": "\"Key strengths:\" lead-in"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[257, 257]], "assertion": "large sample size (100,135 dyads, 1,227 players) cited as a strength", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[258, 258]], "assertion": "high-quality skin tone measurement (independent raters, r=0.923) cited as a strength", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone measurement"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[259, 259]], "assertion": "appropriate statistical methods (cluster-robust SE, marginal standardization) cited as a strength", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["statistical methods"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[260, 260]], "assertion": "comprehensive covariate adjustment cited as a strength", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[261, 262]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses cited as supporting robustness", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[263, 263]], "note": "\"Key limitations:\" lead-in"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[264, 264]], "note": "observational design; cannot definitively establish causation"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[265, 265]], "note": "potential unmeasured confounding cited as a limitation"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[266, 266]], "assertion": "missing data: 15% lack skin tone, 7% lack position", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[267, 267]], "assertion": "effect heterogeneity across leagues suggests contextual dependence, cited as a limitation", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league heterogeneity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[268, 269]], "note": "moderate effect size requires cautious interpretation"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[270, 271]], "assertion": "overall assessment: evidence supports the hypothesis though residual confounding and alternative explanations cannot be fully ruled out; findings consistent with implicit racial bias affecting referee decisions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall assessment"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[272, 273]], "note": "section separator"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[274, 275]], "note": "Technical Appendix heading"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[276, 276]], "note": "Data Source subheading"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[277, 278]], "note": "dataset provenance: sports statistics company, 146,028 dyads, England/Germany/France/Spain 2012-2013, 2,053 players, 3,147 referees"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[279, 279]], "note": "Reproducibility subheading"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[280, 283]], "assertion": "complete analysis code is provided in final_analysis.py and results can be reproduced by running it", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility", "final_analysis.py"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[284, 285]], "note": "Software subheading"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[286, 292]], "assertion": "specific software versions were used: Python 3.11, pandas 2.0+, statsmodels 0.14+, numpy 1.24+, scipy 1.10+, matplotlib 3.7+", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software versions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[293, 294]], "note": "section separator"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[295, 295]], "note": "report generation date line"}]}}